// BrightSprouts Academy: real facts for the Flora & Fauna globe's country hover card.
//
// Every field here is sourced, not recalled: description and photo from the country's own
// Wikipedia article (photo actually comes from the CAPITAL city's article, since country
// articles mostly lead with a flag, a coat of arms, or a locator map rather than a real
// photo of the place); the fun fact is the country's real highest point and elevation from
// Wikidata (P610/P2044), the same structured-data standard the species photos use. One
// country (the Gambia) has no highest-point claim in Wikidata, so it falls back to population.
//
// Border-count trivia was tried and dropped: Wikidata's "shares border with" property mixes
// land and maritime neighbours, which would have told a child Japan borders 6 countries.
//
// Written without em dashes.
